-5ed2-b885-814c97b7c2c5" 13194139533869 true] [17592186262521 1145 "Let $R$ be the event that the chosen marble is red, and let $A$ be the event that the marble was selected from box $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the marble was selected from box $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected marble is red, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(R)=P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the marbles are in box $A$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ are in box $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{3}{4},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the marbles in box $A$ are red, we have\n\n$$\nP(R|A)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{7}{10}$ of the marbles in both boxes are red, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(R|{A}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =(\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{3}{4})+P(R|{A}^{′})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}P(R|{A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}P(R|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ P(R|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected marble from box $B$ is red is $\\frac{4}{5}.$" 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262523 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262524 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262525 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262526 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262527 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1041 "selection" 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262523 13194139533869 true] [17592186262522 1110 #uuid "b5d5d8d4-e0fd-5890-943c-90195